.SS Configuration
.TP
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rustyfi/config.toml ", " ~/.config/rustyfi/config.toml
Your own settings; `$RUSTYFI_CONFIG_DIR` overrides where this is looked for.
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/rustyfi/config.toml
The defaults shipped with the install, found as
.IR <executable>/../share/rustyfi .
Consulted last, so a config you wrote always wins.
.SH STAGING
A program runs in two stages. Stage 1 is the document stage, which produces the
PDF and is where a
.I .saty
file's own code lives; stage 0 runs before it and builds stage-1 code.
.B &e
quotes: it does not run
.IR e ,
it yields a value standing for it.
.B ~e
splices, running
.I e
one stage earlier and inserting the resulting code value at that point. The two
are inverses. A quote is legal only at stage 0, a splice only at stage 1, and a
stage-0 binding cannot be named from stage 1: only
.B persistent
crosses.
.PP
SATySFi 0.0 declares one stage per file, with a
.BI @stage: " persistent|0|1"
header; 0.1 declares it per binding, as
.B val ~x
(stage 0) or
.B val persistent ~x
(persistent), a plain
.B val x
being stage 1. The type a quote produces is written
.BI code " <type>"
in 0.1, which 0.0 has no spelling for.
.PP
One deviation from upstream: upstream resolves every splice in a preprocessing
pass before any stage-1 code runs, whereas here a splice runs where it stands.
The value is the same for pure code-building; the two differ only for side
effects interleaved with stage-1 code.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT
Library root, when
.B \-\-lib\-root
is not given.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_FONT_DIR
Font root, when
.B \-\-font\-dir
is not given.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base of the compile-cache directory.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_OFFLINE
Make the package manager fail cleanly instead of reaching the network.
.TP
.B RUSTYFI_REGISTRY_TOKEN
Bearer token for registry tarball downloads over HTTP.
.SH FILES
When no root is named, ALL of these are searched, in this order, from the
document's own directory (or, for
.BR satyrographos ,
the working directory) upward and then outward \(em so a project-local root
adds to the wider ones rather than replacing them. Naming a root with
.B \-\-lib\-root
or
.B $RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT
searches that one alone.
.TP
.I <dir>/lib\-rustyfi/
A checked-out source tree \(em development.
.TP
.I <dir>/.rustyfi/
A project-local root, recognised only where a
.I Satyristes
sits beside it.
.TP
.I <prefix>/lib/rustyfi
The install this binary belongs to, found as
.IR <executable>/../lib/rustyfi ,
so an unpacked archive works wherever it sits.
.TP
.IR ~/.local/lib/rustyfi ", " /usr/local/lib/rustyfi ", " /usr/lib/rustyfi
User-wide, then system-wide \(em where a release archive unpacks to.
.PP
Inside whichever root is chosen:
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/packages/
SATySFi 0.0 packages.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist\-v01/packages/
SATySFi 0.1 packages.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/fonts/
Bundled font files, each with its licence beside it.
.TP
.I <lib\-root>/dist/hash/fonts.rustyfi\-hash
Maps a font name used by a document to the file that provides it;
.I default\-font.rustyfi\-hash
names the regular, bold, oblique and math defaults.
.TP
.I <doc>.satysfi\-aux
Cross-reference table, in the same JSON format upstream SATySFi writes, so the
two interoperate.
.SH MATH RENDERING
A document's mathematics is parsed, elaborated, evaluated
.I and laid out
during compilation, so what reaches a non-PDF backend is positioned glyphs and
a few filled paths \(em there is no
.B \efrac
node left to serialize. Every rendering below is therefore a recovery from
geometry, and which one suits depends on where the file will be read. The four
are mutually exclusive; all four are an error with
.BR "\-\-format pdf" ,
which typesets the equation itself, and with
.BR "\-\-format latex" ,
which always writes the LaTeX
.B \-\-katex
asks for \(em a
.I .tex
reaches a math typesetter by definition, so every other rendering would only
lose structure it can keep.
.TP
.B \-\-svg\-outline\-math
Each glyph as an SVG outline path from the document's own face, with the
characters kept behind it as invisible selectable text. Reproduces the PDF
exactly and needs nothing of the reader. Largest output.
.B The default for \-\-format html.
.TP
.B \-\-svg\-math
SVG
.B <text>
for the glyphs and
.BR <rect> / <line>
for fraction bars and rules, at the positions the layout computed. Compact,
with real selectable text and a readable source; depends on the reader having
the document's faces. A MATH-table variant glyph \(em a display-size
summation, a stretched delimiter \(em has no character that names it and keeps
an outline path.
.B The default for \-\-format markdown.
.TP
.B \-\-katex
LaTeX in math delimiters
.RB ( $...$ / $$...$$
in Markdown,
.BR \e(...\e) / \e[...\e]
in HTML \(em the delimiters KaTeX's auto-render and MathJax enable by
default), for a reader whose renderer typesets it.
.B Re-derived, not round-tripped:
radicals, delimiters drawn as paths, matrices, nested fractions and nested
scripts do not come back, and a symbol with no name in the table is written as
its own character. Suitable where the equation's structure matters more than
its exact appearance.
.TP
.B \-\-unicode\-math
The characters in reading order, using Unicode's own super/subscripts where
they exist and splitting a fraction at its bar. The only rendering that is
plain
.IR text :
it survives any renderer, reads in a terminal and is greppable. Markdown only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success;
.B 2
for a usage error, including a math flag given with a format that has no
reading for it;
.B 1
if the document fails to load, typecheck, evaluate or render; and a non-zero
code if a package operation fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compile a document with the packages and fonts from an unpacked release:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ export RUSTYFI_LIB_ROOT=/opt/rustyfi/lib/rustyfi
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-o doc.pdf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Publish the same document as a reflowable web page, check the layout in a
browser, and see where the time goes:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-format html
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-format markdown \-\-katex
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-timing
.EE
.RE
.PP
Hand it to another typesetter instead. The generated preamble names the engine
it needs \(em any of the three where the document has no CJK in it, lualatex
where it has:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ rustyfi doc.saty \-\-format latex \-o doc.tex
$ lualatex doc.tex
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and manual, and upstream SATySFi:
.UR https://github.com/gfngfn/SATySFi
.UE .
